the paperwork  i hope this works out  there's nothing missing and really  nothing can be missing  i've already been in contact with the  people from the district office a lot of  back and forth and they've already  opened a file for them everything should  be okay  they've been waiting for this  appointment for weeks  are you registered with the state of  berlin yet  yes could be that i have it with me  they're missing the confirmation the  interpreter helps them search through  their emails again  and luckily they track down the right  one  it's a bit nerve-wracking making sure  that absolutely nothing is missing  we have a great feeling  because as far as i understand it we'll  receive the money directly afterwards  and that takes the pressure off  are surprised how quickly everything is  going  germany has removed many bureaucratic  hurdles for ukrainian refugees  the pair can collect their money  directly it's about 350 euros per person  which they'll start receiving every  month  [Music]  i'm glad everything went so fast  we're exhausted  all that running around  and then you stand there waiting and  wondering whether it will all work out  or not  i'm feeling hopeful now that everything  went so smoothly  to integrate even better ann and zachary  have signed up for a german course  a church congregation organizes weekly  lessons free of charge  after a short introduction they start  practicing  what is the name of your wife your  husband  is  it's a little bit difficult  but it's okay  we are teach  teaching  so we are students we want to study  germany  payetta  are among 60 000 refugees from ukraine  now living in berlin  they often see ukrainian flags across  the city a sign of solidarity  today the two are on their way to the  ukrainian embassy in berlin  they want to lay your roles for anna's  father  [Music]  he died early on in this war  he died five years ago while fighting in  eastern ukraine the war has been going  on since 2014  since russia's annexation of crimea  [Music]  it's good that there's somewhere in  berlin where ukrainians can come to  express their grief and leave it in this  place  the children who have been killed are  commemorated here with drawings candles  and flowers  [Music]  bye  [Music]  a few weeks later sasha and anna want to  show their things  they're preparing a meal for their hosts  catherine is learning how to make a  traditional ukrainian beetroot soup  a ukrainian cooking class today sasha a  master classic  [Music]  this is our ukrainian national dish  it really fills you up  today we're making it with lots of beans  to replace the meat but a real ukrainian  borscht is cooked with meat with pork  ribs  the borscht brings back memories  anna has not seen her family and friends  for weeks  some are still in chennai if others like  her have fled abroad or are still in  transit  i want to see my grandparents and eat  grand  grandmother's food  because  it's  the most beautiful thing in the world  and  meet my friend  and talk about  how they're feeling and everything is  fine or  maybe something is terrible  and just talk  are settling into their new lives  they get along well with their host  family and know that they can stay with  them as long as they want  delicious  very tasty  it feels like we're having dinner with  our own family  we're already totally comfortable with  our german family it's like being at  home  [Music]  the mother and daughter are slowly  finding their bearings in berlin  together they're discovering a new  country a new culture  before they fled they'd never been  outside ukraine  since they've arrived they've grown even  closer together  anna feels so comfortable she can even  imagine studying here right now she's  wrapping up her high school final exams  online  i want to  to come back to ukraine to see my  family members but i think about living  in german  for my life  in the future  because i really like this country  i'm not at the age to completely  overturn my old life all my relatives  are in ukraine and my house too  i want anna to decide for herself  whether she wants to stay in germany or  return to ukraine  but i want to go home someday when the  war is over i will definitely do that  but at the moment they have no idea how  long that will take  [Music]  you

